    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries our highest efficiency score of 77.98. Facing Noah Cameron, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.16 xERA and a positive platoon edge that boosts his raw projection significantly. Joining him at the top of the recommended starts is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), who looks to capitalize on a soft matchup against Hayden Wesneski. The combination of an elevated 4.55 xERA for Wesneski and the strategic positioning of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** in the #3 hole creates a high-ceiling environment for run production. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** (64.61) finds himself in an advantageous spot against the same pitching matchup, with the park and SP skill factors aligning to keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" category.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card involved keeping **Luis Robert Jr.** on the bench with a 39.50 score. While his raw talent is undeniable, the algorithm aggressively penalized his start due to a daunting matchup against Jacob Misiorowski, whose elite 2.14 xERA acts as a hard cap on offensive ceiling. With SB efficiency at a premium, the optimizer opted for **Nasim Nunez** (59.47) instead; despite a lower base projection, **Nasim Nunez** provides essential volume in the scarcity-driven SB category without the extreme risk posed by Misiorowski\u2019s profile. Conversely, **Kyle Tucker** (50.63) remains a volatile start today; he is forced to contend with Chris Sale\u2019s elite 2.81 xERA, which effectively neutralized his typically high base score, leaving him as a marginal play despite his pedigree.\n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Drake Baldwin** (51.80) and **Coby Mayo** (49.34). While **Drake Baldwin** receives a healthy bump for his projected leadoff duties against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, he remains tethered to the performance of a high-tier arm; if he drops